      "content": "I just took another close look at the AeroFlow specs vs the 2018 patent. It's looking tougher than I thought—the lattice geometry and the way they integrate the channels into the core looks almost identical to the claims in '789. \n\nI'm feeling a lot of pressure from the client to get this filed by Friday, and they really don't want to hear that their tech might already be public domain. Given how similar they are, do you think we can still make a successful case for novelty by focusing on the efficiency gains, or is that 2018 patent going to be a total dealbreaker? I need your honest professional judgment here before I talk to them.",
